This project contains ports of algorithms from, and was verified against,
the following works. Their licences and notices apply to the corresponding
material.

tiny-skia — https://github.com/linebender/tiny-skia
  Copyright (c) 2020 Yevhenii Reizner. BSD-3-Clause.
  Itself a port of parts of Skia, Copyright (c) 2011 Google Inc., BSD-3-Clause.
  The anti-aliased scan converter (supersampling, coverage accumulation),
  hairline stroking, cubic and quadratic subdivision counts, the dash
  splitting rules, the lowp blend arithmetic and the gradient evaluation in
  this project are fixed-point Lean re-implementations of tiny-skia's
  algorithms (LeanSvg/Raster.lean, Geom.lean, Canvas.lean, Shader.lean).

resvg and usvg — https://github.com/linebender/resvg
  Copyright (c) 2017 Yevhenii Reizner. MPL-2.0.
  Used as the rendering oracle in the test harness and as the reference for
  SVG semantics (parsing defaults, conditional processing, CSS cascade,
  paint servers, text layout). No resvg or usvg source code is included in
  this project; behaviour was matched by reading it. The resvg test suite is
  used locally for fidelity measurement and is not distributed here.

simplecss — https://github.com/linebender/simplecss
  Copyright (c) 2019 Yevhenii Reizner. MIT/Apache-2.0.
  The supported CSS selector subset in LeanSvg/Css.lean follows its grammar.

Lean 4 and Lake — https://github.com/leanprover/lean4
  Apache-2.0. The language, standard library and build tool. No other
  dependency is used: the trusted computing base is Lean core only.

svgtypes — https://github.com/linebender/svgtypes
  Copyright (c) 2018 Yevhenii Reizner. MIT/Apache-2.0.
  Colour, length and transform parsing rules follow its behaviour.

Noto Sans — https://github.com/notofonts/latin-greek-cyrillic
  Copyright 2022 The Noto Project Authors. SIL Open Font License 1.1
  (LeanSvg/Fonts/LICENSE-OFL.txt). Latin subsets of Noto Sans Regular,
  Bold and Italic are embedded in the binary as LeanSvg/Fonts/*.lean.

lean-zip — https://github.com/kim-em/lean-zip
  Copyright Kim Morrison. Apache-2.0. The "one input, one output, proven
  effect boundary" project shape follows its example; no code is shared.

Used only when running the tests, cloned locally and not distributed with
this project: the resvg binary as the rendering oracle (MPL-2.0), the resvg
test suite (MPL-2.0), simple-icons (CC0-1.0), Feather icons (MIT), Pillow
(MIT-CMU), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause), fontTools (MIT). If a published page or
release ever includes renders derived from the resvg test suite, that
material is MPL-2.0 and must carry the suite's licence and state that the
files are unmodified.

